      "side": 1,
      "message": "This needs to support the case where newLp.getCaptivePortalData() is non-null, but gets updated with new data (happens often if the portal goes from open to closed, or the remaining bytes change for example).\n\nIt should also support the case where the captive portal data sent by NetworkMonitor becomes null after being non-null.\n\nI think processLinkPropertiesFromAgent would be a good place to do that: you can add a \"networkAgentPortalData\" member to NetworkAgentInfo, set it in processLinkPropertiesFromAgent, and rename captivePortalData to capportApiData.\nThen in this method, you just merge the two, by taking all non-empty fields from either (*technically* it\u0027s possible for both to be used).",
